as it has come down to us.=A0 Panini's grammar is more prescriptive than de=
scriptive, at least as it came to be used. As for assimilation, the rules i=
n Panini prescribe what assimilation takes place (all the obvious ones and =
some rather surprising ones), so that any deviation from this is just bad S=
anskrit (Nehru, I think it was, was looked down on by many Brahmins because=
 his Sanskrit had an Uttar Pradeshi accent).=A0 I'm not sure that accidenta=
l assimilations in Lojban would be so terrible, but they might in some case=
s ruin the isomorphism -- better to insert a y or whatever than that.



